Message-ID: <CRZOdA_OOEI.NTxX5ZvBBwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <CRZOdA_OOEI.qfp-pF2ICQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <CRZOdA_OOEI.qfp-pF2ICQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/CRZOdA_OOEI/m/NTxX5ZvBBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The main limit is the size of your RAM.
If you're running on a multicore system, then reducing the number of allowed threads (num.threads in the inla() call) will reduce the required memory.

Finn

